00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:54.380
them i think we ought to give it a try there's some mighty fine boys back around uh bug tussle

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:59.970
silver dollar city besides we's lonesome for the hills mighty pretty back there this

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.890
time of the year, leaves turning.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:04.190
Well, you'll come back right away, won't you?

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:06.620
I kind of like to do a little trout fishing

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:08.400
with old Jim Owen. He knows where them

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:10.420
big rascals hide out. And you can go

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:12.660
hunting and get me a brace of wild

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:15.800
turkeys for Thanksgiving. Thanksgiving?

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:18.220
The best hunting is right after the first

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:20.220
snowfall. Oh, Jed, let's stay

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:21.440
for a white Christmas.

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:25.010
Christmas? My favorite time of year

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:26.950
back home is when the dogwood

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:28.030
blooms in the spring.

00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:29.260
Spring?

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:32.900
It's hard to be summer in them cool woods.

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:33.720
Summer?

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:35.700
That makes a whole year.

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:37.050
That's right.

00:17:37.270 --> 00:17:38.870
Time sure flies in the hills.

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:41.540
A year would only tease us.

00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:43.520
Let's just stay there.

00:17:57.120 --> 00:17:58.020
Don't draft.

00:17:58.890 --> 00:17:59.590
Did you get that?

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:03.340
So I took this away from a fella.

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:05.080
What happened to your pretty dress?

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:07.570
Well, I traded it for these groovy threads

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:09.130
that I got to camp for Flop Shop.

00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:10.380
Flop Shop?

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:12.560
I think she means Swap Shop.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:14.060
Come with me.

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:15.040
Where are we going?

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:16.180
Back home to the hill.

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:19.430
You are gonna beat Big Mount Bradshaw to the altar.

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:22.620
Hey, soul cousin.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.840
Did Ellie tell you about the raid on a college cafeteria?

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:28.400
Wiped them out. Ain't got a bit of food left.

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:29.880
Well, it sounds like a mob.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.720
How many were there?

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:31.560
Me.

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:34.480
Well, Jed, baby, that college life is a gas.

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:35.880
I mean, that's where it's happening.

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:39.680
Don't sound like you're happening to learn, but...

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:41.130
Not true, old-timer.

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:42.520
We's learning the three R's.

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:44.620
Rioting, raiding, and ransacking.

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:49.590
Poor old cat just don't dig.

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:51.020
So far out, it's pitiful.

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:52.540
I mean, come on, Dad.

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:53.360
Like, get with it.

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:54.430
Clean a little, Pops.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:55.780
Lay some skin on me.

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:59.070
You know, I might just do that.

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:02.390
Bless his sweet old heart.

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:04.020
Or just to a different drummer.

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:06.670
I ain't blaming you old folks.

00:19:06.970 --> 00:19:08.130
It's the generation gap.

00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:09.850
But I gotta do what I gotta do.

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:12.220
I'm tuned in, turned on, and toned up.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:15.600
Well, tune out, turn off, and pack up.

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:16.690
We're going home.

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:19.220
Is he kidding?

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:20.520
I ain't going back to the hills.

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:21.580
I'm a college man.

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:24.890
I'm gonna stay right here where I got intellectual freedom.

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:26.550
You're absolutely right, Jethro.

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:28.560
You don't want to be a college dropout.

00:19:28.720 --> 00:19:29.360
I sure don't.

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:29.980
College is...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:34.390
fun there's lots of fellas and lots of girls and quick as i can learn to tell them apart it's going

00:19:34.390 --> 00:19:44.720
to be a lot more fun boy let's get these bags on the truck and are you hurry and pack while i put

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:50.710
up some lunch for the rope i ain't going granny what did you say i ain't going back to the hills

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:56.500
i want to stay right here and pursue my education well gee whiz jethro if when you don't drive the

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:58.440
truck? It can't none of us go.

00:19:59.370 --> 00:19:59.850
What's this?

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:01.400
Not going back to the hills.

00:20:01.580 --> 00:20:03.000
Oh, what a shame.

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:05.620
Mr. Hannaway, let's give the crampons a hand,

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:07.400
get these bags upstairs and unpacked.

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:10.530
You giving us any thought?

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:12.140
Yes, sir.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:14.580
Talk the whole thing over with Mr. Drysdale.

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:16.790
I'm going to be a college graduate, just like him,

00:20:16.890 --> 00:20:18.090
and hold down a white-collar job.

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:19.490
Is that so?

00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:20.550
Yes, sir.

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:22.280
I don't need to work with my hands,

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:24.280
plowing fields and busting stumps.

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:25.680
I'm going to use my head.

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:29.220
You go along with us, do you, Mr. Drysdale?

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:29.970
Mr.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.410
Clabbit, honesty demands that I reply in the affirmative.

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:38.210
This fine boy has a great potential.

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:39.590
I'm proud of him.

00:20:39.690 --> 00:20:40.530
I believe in him.

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:43.360
Oh, I only wish I had a boy just like him.

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:44.430
You got him.

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:45.650
What?

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:52.000
We're going to leave this fine boy, great potential, with you.

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:56.780
Jane, could you drive us to the airport and get us on a plane to home?

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:59.050
Yes, I guess so.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:20:59.330
Come on, Granny.

00:20:59.530 --> 00:20:59.630
Everybody.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:00.200
Let's go.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:01.240
Now, just a minute.

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:03.480
I was, I didn't mean to take my dad there.

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:04.120
Let him go.

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:06.220
Or can I call you dad?

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:07.360
Nuts.

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:08.380
Okay.

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:09.220
Come on, nuts.

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:11.200
You can fix vittles for me and the critters

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:13.000
whilst we talk about my great potential.

00:21:16.490 --> 00:21:22.540
The cat boots black belt.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:24.820
Bad news for the bad guys.

00:21:25.060 --> 00:21:26.340
Walker, Texas Ranger.

00:21:26.740 --> 00:21:28.980
Weeknights at 6 on the Hallmark Channel.

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:29.830
Tomorrow.

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:31.220
I'm taking a kick.

00:21:31.380 --> 00:21:34.400
Don't miss Hallmark Channel's Matlock Movie Marathon.

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:35.380
Everybody be cool.

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:36.540
You're out of your mind.

00:21:36.860 --> 00:21:41.240
Watch Matlock as he cracks the case in a full day of killer thrillers.

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:42.800
Whatever you do, don't lie.

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:43.770
I hate that.

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:48.890
The Matlock Movie Marathon, tomorrow starting at 1 on the Hallmark Channel.

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:50.620
I'll come back now.

00:21:50.800 --> 00:21:51.040
Yeah?
